<title>UK: Canadian Insurance, ABN AMRO end talks.</title>
<headline>Canadian Insurance, ABN AMRO end talks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Insurance Group Limited (CIGL), the majority shareholder of Capel-Cure Myers Capital Management Limited, said on Tuesday that its talks with Capel-Cure minority shareholders and ABN AMRO Hoare Govett about a potential change in ownership have been terminated.</p>
<p>CIGL said it and its majority investor, Credit Suisse First Boston are reviewing with Capel-Cure's management alternative plans for the strategic development of the group.</p>
<p>In March, Capel-Cure and Dutch banking giant ABN AMRO Holding NV's ABN AMRO Hoare Govett said they were in talks that could lead to an offer for Capel-Cure. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
